  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 PM EDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\n\n- Chance of showers and isolated thunderstorms through Sunday\n\nLight showers are all that is currently moving through the region\nas quasi stationary front continues to keep a weakening MCV south\nof Michigan. The stable air over southern Michigan should \ncontinue to stifle convection. As a SFC low moves eastward this \nafternoon and evening it could move north enough to allow for \nscattered showers and isolated storms along the I-94 corridor. \nThe shear and CAPE remain through IN and Ohio so the threat of \nsevere from any storms to forms continues to diminish. Any showers\nand storms that form will be aided by the humid air mass and \nheavy rainfall will be possible. \n\nA short upper level wave and a deepening mid level trough will \nswing a frontal system through the area tomorrow. This could allow\nfor another chance for showers tomorrow morning into early \nafternoon. While lapse rates aren't great and the front is coming \nat the wrong time of day for convection, there should be \nsufficient CAPE and PWATS are upwards of 2 inches from latest \nCAMS. So any showers or storms that do form could have periods of \nheavy rain. \n    \n- Drier and less humid through early part of week\n\nThe front will move through tomorrow with cooler and drier air in\nits wake which will drop Temps and dewpoints down to normal \nmaking the are more comfortable. Max temperatures will be near \nnormal, in the low 80s, through Tuesday. \n\n- Another frontal system could bring showers and storms midweek\n\nThe quasi stationary high that was sitting over the south and \nallowed for all the weather to move through Illinois and Indiana \nthis past week will shift to the west. This upcoming week will be \ndominated by a large upper level low that will build over the \nHudson Bay. A it treks to the east will should move south over \nnorthern Ontario and a cold front extending from it should move \nfrom the northwest, across Michigan and sweep into the mid \nAtlantic by Thursday. There is some question on timing but \ncurrently, there is the potential for showers and storms Tuesday \nnight into Wednesday. This should also clear temperatures off for \nthe latter half of this upcoming week.",
